  "body": "This adds a scoped negative certificate for adjacent 2\u21923 Steinberg expansions in PR589\u2019s bit word. Adding a corrective XOR can sometimes reduce frame costs, but it cannot do so in the fixed neighboring contexts examined here. No new \u03ba and no new supplier are claimed.\n\n**Exact result**\n\nFlatten phase A in the pinned source-list order. For every adjacent noncommuting pair on three distinct registers, reverse the pair and insert its corrective gate in each of the three valid positions. Allow arbitrary nested rational intermediate subspaces of Q^8 while fixing surrounding contacts, COPYs and the hosting remainder.\n\nThe complete census contains:\n\n- 316 eligible pairs among 2,130 elementary phase-A gates.\n- 948 corrective orders and 1,671 feasible rank triples.\n- 982 identical paid profiles, 689 strictly worse profiles, zero improvements.\n- 19 distinct histogram deltas.\n- 1,898 forward/inverse scalar replays on all 661 dirty-input basis columns.\n\nA rational flag-completion argument reduces the entire intermediate-subspace domain to these rank triples. Exact truncated-rank inequalities prove the cost comparison simultaneously for every exponent 0 < a < 1. The retained positive per-child fallback charge cannot decrease either.\n\nEntry and exit climbs, source accesses, COPYs and restoration are accounted for. Rebuilding literal cleanup increases the full explicit ADD count from 24,305 to 24,307. The baseline local profile has rank mass 5,129; the nine-stage model remains:\n\nH = 288 * local + {2:13920, 4:14208, 6:14208, 7:21312, 42:288},\nm = 64, W = 28416, deficit = 10272.\n\n**Relationship to prior and concurrent work**\n\nIan Lib\u00e2nio\u2019s PR933 already remarks that inverse expansions are neutral. This contribution independently corroborates a narrower adjacent, fixed-contact portion using a rational flag proof, an all-exponent concavity certificate and a separately implemented integer checker. It does not introduce the expansion mechanism or subsume PR933\u2019s global reframing work.\n\nPR886 covers fixed-word framing; PR1345, PR1382 and PR1413 study transport classes. The final refresh also examined flemhhh\u2019s PR1048 profile/transport audit and Hanson Sun (@bbMisk)\u2019s PR1520 J3 precision tradeoff. Their scopes differ. No code from these pending packages is imported, and no priority claim is made.\n\n**Starting point and pins**\n\nExact starting commit:\n92da4d718f1d4cf8de4e6ee947ddc7b180ce1c31\n\nPR589 source head:\na5afc8c6169ea61ba7c51dfd3cade02cc7b13b46\n\nThe four declared source inputs are pinned by Git blob and SHA256 in SOURCES.json:\n\n- research/e8-bit-p111-tuned/tune/bitE8mut-p111-tuned.json.gz\n  SHA256 e3e301e62bc2b41dbf1ceac0acf3d35824ebeab1848c5a2142d4577b109da52f\n- research/e8-bit-p111-tuned/tune/EXPECTED.json\n  SHA256 b9f0e5ca038abe837b0007c8fe006f366a6f02009244ac57705a8a200e2301f4\n- research/e8-bit-p111-tuned/tune/fastc.py\n  SHA256 ae51f1fbb22b8c8dac8aab787c798361f6aa5d4e1fefb29e43d0197899d4eab5\n- research/e8-bit-carrier-skeleton/code/hub/e8-r740-replica32/code/engines/moment.py\n  SHA256 81cbc864e106418fc7854322746f72180cb8110ff39f74450a3b8d55a82c1482\n\nThe pricing sources bind the accounting references; neither checker imports them.\n\nPR933 was read at b9348c6907516e55dc07e135ad4d7a480d4f9840. Final upstream refresh reached ef5f39403610d231a0c27e8a6b4f08c10209bcd6; all four inputs and the selected record were unchanged.\n\nThe accepted conditional \u03ba remains 0.001672660197076918, with the complex supplier binding. The selected certificate was followed to its actual assembly, manifest and maintainer review.\n\n**Reproduction and executed checks**\n\nRecommended command from the repository root, using Python 3.12 and only its standard library:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/bit589-steinberg-fan-seed06/verify.py\n```\n\nExpected final line:\n\n```text\nPASS_BIT589_STEINBERG_FAN pairs=316 orders=948 rank_schedules=1671 improving=0 controls=8 no_new_kappa\n```\n\nExecuted on Linux with CPython 3.12.14:\n\n- Complete rational census and certificate regeneration: PASS.\n- Independent integer-kernel geometry and sorted-rank majorization checker: PASS.\n- All 1,898 full scalar replays, including COPY/ERASE and cleanup: PASS.\n- Optimized test_package.py: all 18 tests PASS.\n- Registered research_package.py hook: PASS.\n- Fresh source-only export, run outside the checkout with -I -O -B: PASS.\n- Source-binding baseline and Git whitespace checks: PASS.\n\nControls reject omitted gates, incorrect order, wrong subspace containment, unpaid climbs, missing scatter reads, omitted cleanup, source drift and corrupted certificate coverage/geometry/cost fields. A genuinely improving boundary fixture outside this domain is detected. Recompressed certificates are accepted by decoded content.\n\nOne early mutation test made no actual mutation; that fixture was corrected, and mutation tests now verify that their inputs changed. No final test failures remain.\n\n**Scope and unfinished obligations**\n\nThis is a computer-assisted result for one precisely defined local relaxation, not proof-assistant verification or a full multiplication theorem. Arbitrary rational frames relax physical admission; their realizability is not asserted.\n\nNonadjacent rewrites, interacting expansions, global reframing, alternative flattening orders, new helpers, COPY changes and changed hosting are outside scope. Native multistage replay, hosted emission, full frontier1094 replay and remote CI were not run because no candidate improved the favorable rank budget.\n\nThe inherited all-size/compiler, common-label/mutable-source, hosting, precision/tape and analytic assumptions remain unchanged. Public overlap searches were partial, not proof of novelty. Posting access was unavailable; the claim and completed-result update are recorded locally in CLAIM.json.\n\n**Attribution**\n\nPrepared for @CubeJerry with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in research, proof, implementation, verification and writing. Two implementations do not constitute independent human review.\n\nCredit DreamingOfClouds for PR589; eumemic for PR555/R420 and the earlier complex expansion; Dugongue and Rohan Arun for the circuit/cost lineage; SethBurkart123 for PR886; and Ian Lib\u00e2nio for PR933. Concurrent work is credited above and pinned in the package.\n\nNew work is Apache-2.0. Only this research package is added; predecessor sources and the selected frontier are unchanged.",
